fbsdkpi: si_meminfo() reports the machine's memory, not a constant 4 GiB

sf_lkpi_physmem() was a constant. It now asks the xnu seam (sfos_physmem(): hw.memsize; that
function is in patch 0002's files). Found by m1-lkpi-extras: the Asahi driver sizes its GPU
memory limits from totalram.
UPSTREAM: yes.

--- a/src/Kernel/fbsdkpi/sf/lkpi/sf_lkpi_kern.c
+++ b/src/Kernel/fbsdkpi/sf/lkpi/sf_lkpi_kern.c
@@ -72,11 +72,18 @@
 	sfos_sleep_us(1);
 }
 
+uint64_t sfos_physmem(void);
+
 unsigned long
 sf_lkpi_physmem(void)
 {
-	// in pages, linuxkpi only sizes caches from it
-	return (unsigned long)(4ULL << 30) / PAGE_SIZE;
+	// in pages: si_meminfo() totalram, which drivers size their limits from (the Asahi
+	// driver: 67 % of it device-wide, 50 % per client). 4 GiB when xnu does not say.
+	uint64_t bytes = sfos_physmem();
+
+	if (bytes == 0)
+		bytes = 4ULL << 30;
+	return (unsigned long)(bytes / PAGE_SIZE);
 }
 
 char *
